# Regional Structure

All code must be organized using regional dividers for clear structure and code folding support.

## JavaScript Regions

```javascript
// #Region ------------------------------------------------
// BLOCK TYPE | Description
// --------------------------------------------------------

    // Content here (4-space indent - CRITICAL for code folding)

// endregion ----------------------------------------------
```

**Block Types:** MODULE, FUNCTION, SUB FUNCTION, HELPER FUNCTION, CLASS, METHOD, DATA, CONSTANTS, STATE, API, EVENTS, INITIALIZATION

**Dash Counts:** Opening (60), Section (56 with indent), Closing (50)

---

## CSS Regions

```css
/*  #Region ------------------------------------------------
 * BLOCK TYPE | Description
 * -------------------------------------------------------- */

    /* CSS rules (4-space indent) */

/* endregion ---------------------------------------------- */
```

**Dash Counts:** Opening (60), Section (56 with indent), Closing (50)

---

## HTML Regions

```html
<!-- #Region ------------------------------------------ -->
<!-- BLOCK TYPE | Description                          -->
<!-- ----- -->

    <!-- UI COMPONENT | Description                     -->
    <!-- --- -->
    <div id="component">
        <!-- Content -->
    </div>
    <!-- --- -->

<!-- endregion ---------------------------------------- -->
```

**Dash Counts:** Opening (65), Subsection (57 with indent), Closing (60)

---

## Regional Structure Components

Each region has three parts:

1. **Opening Tag** - Marks region start (includes `#Region` for code folding)
   - JavaScript: 60 chars total
   - CSS: 60 chars total  
   - HTML: 65 chars total

2. **Section Divider** - Separates header from content
   - JavaScript: 56 dashes (with 4-space indent)
   - CSS: 56 dashes (with 4-space indent)
   - HTML: Uses BLOCK TYPE line instead

3. **Closing Tag** - Marks region end
   - JavaScript: 50 dashes
   - CSS: 50 dashes
   - HTML: 60 dashes

### Block Type Labels

Use specific descriptive labels based on context:
- **JavaScript/CSS:** MODULE, FUNCTION, HELPER FUNCTION, CLASS, METHOD, DATA, CONSTANTS, STATE, API, EVENTS, INITIALIZATION
- **HTML:** REGION (for major sections), UI HEADER, UI NAVIGATION, UI MAIN, UI SECTION, UI PANEL, UI MODAL, UI FOOTER

---

## Rules

### ALWAYS
- Use 4-space indent within ALL regions (critical for code folding)
- Region type in CAPS before pipe separator
- Close every region with `endregion`
- Use correct dash counts per file type

### NEVER
- Skip 4-space indent (breaks code folding)
- Use inconsistent dash counts
- Forget to close regions
- Use tabs instead of spaces
